"# Oh boy\nFrodoe old Frodoe old\n- Went out to do some final cleaning of yesterdays setup\n- The plan was for all four of us to go out and finish up, to make sure Lincoln did something to help\n- Lincoln’s dying his hair; red, I guess\n- Me and dad \\(speaking for myself and assuming for him\\) just wanted to deal with the stuff instead of standing around waiting\n- \\(I much prefer lying my sore body in bed right now\\)\n- So we went outside and started moving things down to the shed\n- And mom comes out and, as one might expect, she’s at a 7 or an 8 when she should be at a 3\n- Telling us the stuff we were taking down wasn’t supposed to be taken down, but also we were supposed to be waiting for “El”\n- Which is great and all, but her patented “you idiots” tone was unnecessary\\. Coming out swinging was unnecessary\\. Because obviously dad swings back\\. Not literally, I feel I should say\\. But that’s his default\\.\n- But don’t come out swinging when we’re just trying to do a job\\. \n- Don’t light the fire under the guy perpetually already almost at a boil\\.\n- And then I moved a couple chairs that *were* supposed to go, and came back\n- \\(EDIT: oh right \\- while I was down there, I heard her deliver her “don’t get mad at me” line\\. Good god damn\\. \\)\n- And I guess by that point she’d become impatient and said let’s just finish it\n- And I made sure to ask the clarifying question of exactly what “it” is and got enough tone in her “move the table” response that me and dad both snapped back simultaneously\n- Myself with a snappy “I know, ok, I just\\.\\.\\.\\.” dumb crap like that\\. I’m not used to being cogently angry when my parents are involved\\. Or at all?\n- Dad with, I’m pretty sure, a “GO AWAY” that got ignored or missed or something\\.\n- So then we finished the job, and Lincoln never came out, and that was that\\. \n- I think she got the hint at that point, because everyone dialed everything back after that point\\. \n- But none of the high tension bullcannoli was necessary\\. \n- Her default tone for “wait, not those ones, bring those back” is critical and sharp and annoyed\\. \n- It’s a *bad look* when we’re just trying to help\\. \n- And when she starts at a 7 or an 8, dad jumps to a 10 immediately, because he’s always near boiling point\\. \n- And when they both do their thing, ​*the air changes*​\\.\n- How is it that such a caustic, volatile combination has stayed married for 30\\+ years\\. \n- If they ever divorce\\.\\.\\.\\. boy\\. It’s not gonna affect me at all, I guess\\. I’ll be gone, and I won’t exactly not understand why it’s happening\\. But then, of course, I’ll probably be called on to be comforting to both of them\\.\\.\\.\\.\n- I doubt they’ll ever divorce\\. They’re mostly fine and i don’t see either of them diving into the approaching\\-retirement\\-age dating pool\\. \n- EDIT: and they just bought a house\n- But beautiful do they both know how to kick up a needless, stupid conflict\\. \n\n- Tonight’s dinner was leftovers from the last couple days\\. Dog and burger, plus chateau bread and fries\\. Mom had eaten the last of the Mac and cheese, which is fair because I guess she didn’t get any yesterday\\. \n"
